From 720c1f8245014bb5d682913845a18bbbdf0d9bca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 20:58:31 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Wire PORT_BUILD_SHA12 build fingerprint into RUNMANIFEST's
 binary_sha12

Patch 0038 wired RUNMANIFEST emission at quit()'s clean-shutdown path
but left binary_sha12 empty by design -- no build-fingerprint pipeline
existed yet for this CMake-driven engine stage. This port's own
Makefile now computes AGS_BUILD_SHA12 (a content hash of both vendor
trees post-patch, this stage's own CMake flags, the hub build
fragment, and the compiler version -- see that Makefile's own "Build
fingerprint" section) and threads it through CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS as
-DPORT_BUILD_SHA12="<hash>", following dossage's own BUILD_SHA12
precedent (read directly, not summarized).

Why not leave it empty indefinitely: an unattributable RUNMANIFEST
block can't tell a later analyst which build produced it, the same gap
dossage's own BENCHMARK-PLAN.md documents hitting for real (a pinned
build_sha12 that could not be recomputed or checked).
---
 Engine/main/quit.cpp | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Engine/main/quit.cpp b/Engine/main/quit.cpp
index 2c73bf227..20a11d411 100644
--- a/Engine/main/quit.cpp
+++ b/Engine/main/quit.cpp
@@ -281,6 +281,22 @@ void quit(const char *quitmsg)
         runmanifest_t manifest;
         runmanifest_init(&manifest);
 
+        // DOS-PORT: PORT_BUILD_SHA12 is a content-hash fingerprint of the
+        // inputs that determine this engine-stage binary (both vendor
+        // trees post-patch, this stage's own CMake flags, the hub build
+        // fragment, the compiler version -- see the Makefile's own "Build
+        // fingerprint" section), passed in via -DPORT_BUILD_SHA12 on the
+        // CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS this target compiles with. Left at
+        // runmanifest_init()'s own empty default (not guarded by an
+        // #ifdef) if a future build stage ever omits the flag -- an
+        // honest empty field, per the schema's own documented convention,
+        // rather than a stale or guessed value.
+#ifdef PORT_BUILD_SHA12
+        strncpy(manifest.binary_sha12, PORT_BUILD_SHA12,
+                sizeof(manifest.binary_sha12) - 1);
+        manifest.binary_sha12[sizeof(manifest.binary_sha12) - 1] = '\0';
+#endif
+
         manifest.environment = runmanifest_detect_environment(NULL);
         runmanifest_compute_env_block_sha12(dos_port_env_allowlist,
             manifest.env_block_sha, sizeof(manifest.env_block_sha));
